Subject: [PATCH 3/3] =?UTF-8?q?=E2=9C=A8=20Add=20option=20to=20use=20Class?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ipod=20as=20the=20home=20screen=20on=20Android?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings > Home Screen (Android only) turns it on and off:
- On enables a HOME activity and asks Android, through the system
  "default home app" dialog, to make Classipod the home app. Android 9
  and older open the default home app setting instead.
- Off disables the activity, and Android falls back to the other
  launcher.

The HOME activity only forwards to the normal Classipod activity and
finishes, so the Flutter activity never runs in the home task. That
keeps one activity on audio_service's shared engine, including when the
media notification opens the app.

While Classipod is the home app, Home returns to the main menu, and
Back at the main menu does nothing instead of closing an app Android
would immediately reopen.

